er to November came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, April to May hit 159% of normal and November to December fell to 43%. All 4 grids had their driest year in 2007, with grid 16379 at 53%. A preliminary estimate on grid 16679 puts August to September 2026 at 72.4, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
